A||N||10||Jay||Adventures at Darknights||||1||
Z||000000||Jay||07-12-2001||06:45 PM||||Well, here in Toronto we have an Import and sub compact domestic car show that attracts people from all over North America.  One guy came from California, another from Navada.  It's called Darknights.  This year over 900 cars attended and I was one of only two Fieros.  The other one was entered in the sound competition and had a DVD player in the dash where the heater core unit should be.  <P>All week-end long people were gathering around my car to hear the V8 Northstar start up.  It was great hearing the power of that engine in a sea of sewing machines.  Every time I would start it a crowd would gather around, rubbing their eyes in disbelief.  <P>The judging sucked however.  The guy that judged my car said "Well, I don't know anything about engines so tell me about it" <BR>How the heck did he become a judge for a car show?  I didn't even place in my class "Wild Domestic".  I lost out to a few stock Sunfires with rims and polished intakes and a Cavalier with a tint job.  That sucks, but I'll be back next year.  My moto for the week-end was "EAT RICE".  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||07-12-2001||11:42 PM||||The person judging was probably just a friend of the organizer of the show.  You probably could have told him that your engine was stock  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Too bad there werent more Fieros there.  One thing I want to know about the DVD player in the dash though...why?!?!  It's not like you can watch movies while you drive!  Some people that talk on phones while driving are bad enough!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||07-13-2001||01:26 PM||||Actually, the DVD is pretty cool.  I'm thinking about it for my car.  It would be great for the passenger on long trips or at a car show.  You could pass the time by watching a movie or two.||||reg||1
Z||000003||banditbalz||07-13-2001||07:14 PM||||JAY, who needs a DVD player, when you have certified Northstar entertainment pushing your ass down the road? ha ha haaa<P>Ever consider NOS?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||12
Z||000004||Jay||07-13-2001||09:14 PM||||No NOS, bottles are for babies! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But I am considering a supercharger or turbo!||||reg||1
